   "body": "**Still reproduced, 2026-11-11** (iPhone 18 Pro simulator, iOS 27.0, SwiftHFR @ `9e93c3eb`, logged out, \"[Topik Unik] PokémonGO\" page 1): the first post's header and the top of its first image sit under the top bar.\n\n**Same on the bottom edge**: at the end of a page the last lines of the last message stay under the bottom bar (‹ › and the page button) and cannot be scrolled above it. Legacy stops the content above both bars.\n\nPointer, a hypothesis not measured:\n- Legacy keeps the reader's `WKWebView` on the automatic content inset adjustment (only its SVG viewer sets `.never`, `HFRswift/Swift/MessagesView.swift:7089` @ `87fe0d1c`), with the bottom buttons in `ToolbarItemGroup(placement: .bottomBar)` (`:5611-5649`).\n- SwiftHFR uses the same bar placement (`App/SwiftHFR/Reader/ReaderPageControls.swift:21-36`) but sets `.never` (`ReaderWebController.swift:115`) and applies `obscuredInsets` from SwiftUI (`ReaderWebView.swift:18`, `ReaderWebController+Scroll.swift:17-24`, LOT-186).\n\nIf those insets are wrong or zero on this build, both edges fail, which is what we see. The operator calls the bottom edge a hard point (the legacy fix took time): please treat both edges here, or open a sibling issue for the bottom one.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
